Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `.push()` takes `first`, but `first` is used again later
  --> tests/ui/copies_explicit_element_push.jet:9:16
    |
  9 |     names.push(first)
    |                ^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/copies_explicit_element_push.jet:10:13
    |
 10 |     print("{first} {names.len()}")
    |             ^^^^^ `first` is used again here
 Why: `.push()` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `first` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `first.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `first`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `first`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209
